{"name":"Alarm","hex":"#ec0003","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"alarm","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A summons to arms, as on the approach of an enemy.","Any sound or information intended to give notice of approaching danger; a warning sound to arouse attention; a warning of danger."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To call to arms for defense.","To give (someone) notice of approaching danger or necessary action; to rouse to vigilance; to put on the alert."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/alarm"}],"entries":[{"title":"Alarm","blocks":[{"text":"An alarm is a mechanism that gives an audible, visual, combination, or other kind of alarm signal to alert someone to a problem or condition that requires urgent attention."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Magnuson_Fire_Alarm.jpg/330px-Magnuson_Fire_Alarm.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alarm","wikidata":"Q945434"},{"title":"ALARM","blocks":[{"text":"ALARM is a British anti-radiation missile designed primarily to destroy enemy radars for the purpose of Suppression of Enemy Air Defenses (SEAD). It was used by the RAF and is still used by the Royal Saudi Air Force. The weapon was retired by the UK at the end of 2013."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/ALARM.jpeg/330px-ALARM.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ALARM","wikidata":"Q294350"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Verisure_Moonshot_2022_alarm_system_-_2023-01-03.jpg/500px-Verisure_Moonshot_2022_alarm_system_-_2023-01-03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Verisure_Moonshot_2022_alarm_system_-_2023-01-03.jpg/1280px-Verisure_Moonshot_2022_alarm_system_-_202